    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in 1220 by Ilse Reinegger, Gustav Breidenstein murdered his own sire and spent centuries unifying Germany's Kindred under Berlin's rule, becoming the seat of power for both the mortal nation and its vampires. Committed diablerie is rumored in his past, and his aura no longer bears the stains of the act. His rule as Prince of Berlin was absolute and brutal &mdash; Final Death for failing to present oneself, for breaking Elysium, for breaking the Masquerade &mdash; until his own childe, Wilhelm Waldburg, convinced him to open the city to other clans, then used that opening to seize West Berlin for himself. Gustav now rules only East Berlin as Prince, plotting endlessly to reclaim the whole city and destroy the childe who betrayed him. He was Blood Bound by East Berlin's Brujah during the Cold War and used as a figurehead prince for their designs, a fact that still enrages him privately. His Dominate allows him to affect multiple targets with a touch, and his Presence lets him instill targets with an inescapable sense of purpose and duty.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Give nothing away. Smile only when it serves your interests. Intimidate anyone who questions you. You built Berlin from a hovel in the woods and you are, in a very real sense, Berlin itself.</p>",
    "notes": "Haven: Berlin Palace, East Berlin. All East Berlin Kindred are loyal to Gustav publicly, whether through genuine conviction, Blood Bond, exile, or destruction of dissenters. All Brujah in Berlin support him. Enforces Final Death as the standard punishment for infractions; minor infractions earn a Blood Bond instead. Bitter enemy of Justicar Karl Schrekt and of his own childe Wilhelm Waldburg.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
